<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ publication.name }} — theme proof</title>
<style>
{{ print_css|safe }}
/* The theme compiler emits the saved palette and role font stacks below. */
{{ theme.css|safe }}
html, body { background: #dedbd3; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.proof-sheet {
  width: 11in;
  min-height: 17in;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0.5in 0.5in 0.55in;
  background: var(--paper);
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}
.proof-flag {
  font-family: var(--font-caption);
  font-size: 8pt;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);
  padding-bottom: 3pt;
  margin-bottom: 5pt;
}
.proof-rule { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); margin: 0 0 0.16in; }
.proof-cols { columns: 3; column-gap: 0.24in; column-rule: 1px solid var(--hair); }
.proof-cols p { margin: 0 0 0.075in; text-align: justify; hyphens: auto; }
.proof-specimen { border-top: 2px solid var(--rule); margin-top: 0.16in; padding-top: 5pt; }
.proof-specimen__title {
  font-family: var(--font-section);
  font-weight: var(--section-weight);
  font-size: 8pt;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent);
  margin-bottom: 4pt;
}
.proof-specimen dl { margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1pt 0.3in; }
.proof-specimen dl > div { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8pt; border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--hairline); padding: 2pt 0; }
.proof-specimen dt { color: var(--ink-soft); font-family: var(--font-caption); font-size: 7.4pt; }
.proof-specimen dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-numeric); font-weight: var(--numeric-weight); font-size: 7.4pt; }
.proof-caption {
  font-family: var(--font-caption);
  font-size: 7.4pt;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  padding-top: 3pt;
  margin-top: 0.08in;
}
.proof-footer {
  margin-top: auto;
  border-top: 2px solid var(--rule);
  padding-top: 4pt;
  font-family: var(--font-caption);
  font-size: 7pt;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="proof-sheet">
  <div class="proof-flag">Theme proof · specimen page · not an edition, not a news report</div>
  <header class="masthead">
    <div class="masthead__top"><span>{{ publication.city or "Local edition" }}</span><span>Design proof</span></div>
    <div class="masthead__name">{{ publication.name }}</div>
    <div class="masthead__strap"><span>{{ publication.slogan or "Printed edition" }}</span><span>{{ publication.channel_handle }}</span></div>
  </header>
  <div class="proof-rule"></div>
  <div class="kicker">Specimen · type and colour proof</div>
  <h2 class="story__headline">This page shows how the printed newspaper will look</h2>
  <p class="story__deck">A real render of the saved theme, using the same print stylesheet as the edition.</p>
  <p class="story__standfirst">This specimen is generated by Channel Press so an editor can judge paper tone, ink weight, role fonts and column measure before publishing. It contains no reporting and should never be distributed as an issue.</p>
  <div class="proof-cols story__body">
    <p>The masthead, kicker, headline, deck and standfirst above use the display, headline and standfirst roles selected in Appearance. Body copy uses the selected body face at the chosen size and leading. Small labels and captions use the caption role, while the figures below use the numeric role.</p>
    <p>Colours are applied as ink on the selected paper tone. Rules, hairlines and shaded panels are derived from the same palette, so a dark rule does not force unreadable small text. The accent stays on labels and rules rather than body copy.</p>
    <p>Imported fonts are embedded from the local font library and copied with the proof, the PDF and the e-paper bundle. If an installed family is later removed from this computer, the renderer reports the substitution instead of pretending the original face was used.</p>
    <p>This paragraph deliberately runs long enough to show justified text, hyphenation and the column rule at physical tabloid size. Inspect the proof at 100% zoom: body text should remain legible, and no line should collide with a rule, caption or image edge.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="story__media">
    <div class="locator-fallback" style="min-height:1.25in;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Image area</div>
        <div style="font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:15pt">A source photograph would sit here with its caption and credit.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>Captions use the caption role. Every published image must carry its real source, credit and verification status. <span class="credit">Specimen · no photograph</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <aside class="evidence-box">
    <div class="evidence-box__title">Evidence and provenance box</div>
    <dl>
      <div><dt>Source messages</dt><dd>18</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Claims checked</dt><dd>42</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Corrections</dt><dd>1</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Review items</dt><dd>0</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="evidence-box__note">Specimen figures only. In a real edition this panel describes the evidence behind the printed reports.</p>
  </aside>
  <section class="proof-specimen">
    <div class="proof-specimen__title">Selected roles</div>
    <dl>
      {% for role in theme_roles %}
      <div><dt>{{ role.label }}</dt><dd>{{ role.family }}</dd></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </dl>
  </section>
  <div class="proof-caption">Theme revision {{ theme.revision_id or "draft" }} · hash {{ theme.hash[:12] }} · generated locally. Check colours and type at 100% zoom before publishing.</div>
  <div class="proof-footer"><span>{{ publication.name }}</span><span>Theme proof · {{ theme.hash[:12] }}</span></div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
